From: bridge <bridge@local>
Subject: [PATCH 0005] net/bluetooth: announce mgmt index on first successful
 ioctl open

The vhci controller's automatic power-on at registration can fail (the
MTK transport behind it asserts and reopens its session for a few seconds
right at startup, so the init commands hit HCI timeouts).  Later
`HCIDEVUP` (hciconfig hci0 up) opens the device through the ioctl path,
which never clears HCI_SETUP and never calls mgmt_index_added().  With
HCI_SETUP stuck, READ_INDEX_LIST skips the controller and userspace
(bluetoothd/btmgmt) can never see it, even though the RAW HCI channel
works fine.

Clear HCI_SETUP and announce the index on the first successful open,
whatever path it came through.  For devices whose registration power-on
already succeeded the flag is long cleared, so this is a no-op.

Signed-off-by: bridge <bridge@local>
---
 net/bluetooth/hci_core.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
@@ -1604,7 +1604,17 @@ static int hci_dev_do_open(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 		    hdev->dev_type == HCI_PRIMARY) {
 			ret = __hci_req_hci_power_on(hdev);
 			mgmt_power_on(hdev, ret);
 		}
+
+		/* The first successful open may have come through the
+		 * HCIDEVUP ioctl path (auto power-on at registration
+		 * failed earlier).  Announce the index to mgmt, or
+		 * userspace never sees this controller. */
+		if (hci_dev_test_and_clear_flag(hdev, HCI_SETUP)) {
+			if (hci_dev_test_flag(hdev, HCI_UNCONFIGURED))
+				set_bit(HCI_RAW, &hdev->flags);
+			mgmt_index_added(hdev);
+		}
 	} else {
 		/* Init failed, cleanup */
 		flush_work(&hdev->tx_work);
